  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0173" xml:lang="en">
          <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00519/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_gardner">
              <opener>
                <seg hand="#print_gardner">
                  <placeName>
                    <address>
                        <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_567">10 LYNTON ROAD
                        <lb/>NEW MALDEN
                        <lb/>SURREY
                        <lb/>KT3 5EE</rs>
                    </address>
                  </placeName>
                  <lb/>01-942 7322
                </seg>
                <dateline>  
                  <date>
                    <lb/><space quantity="26" unit="char"/>31-vii-73
                  </date>
                </dateline>
                <salute>
                  <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Mr Auden</rs>,
                </salute>
              </opener>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>Thank you for your letter of 16 July.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>About length of the anti-masque for Cupid and Death.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I'd
                <lb/>have thought about twenty minutes (I've not been given a precise
                <lb/>brief).<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Certainly not longer than half-an-hour.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I'm really
                <lb/>very hazy about what's watned, partly, I think, because noone
                <lb/>seems to know Cupid and Death very well and those who do say the
                <lb/>music is marvellous but the story and staging without interest (which is
                <lb/>a very bad way to plan to put on a dramatic spectacle).<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Obvi-
                <lb/>ously our contribution must have some relevance both to C. and
                <lb/>D. and to our own century.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>The forces involved should be iden-
                <lb/>tical<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>(i.e. SATB soloists, chorus and an orchestra of strings
                <lb/>and harpsichord).<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I am a very light composer these days and 
                <lb/>seek to entertain - myself first, but one or two others are
                <lb/>sometimes appreciative.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I have no ideas, really, on how the
                <lb/>task should be done, except that I'm sure you and Mr Kallman
                <lb/>will do a super job.
              </p>
              <closer>
                <salute>
                  <lb/><space quantity="16" unit="char"/>Yours sincerely,
                </salute>
                <signed hand="#hand_black_gardner">
                  <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_561">John Gardner</rs>
                </signed>
              </closer>
             </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00520/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
            <div>
              <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0173">
                <lb/>81
              </ab>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
    </body>
